- op: discuss  # 12b2
  at: '2026-08-26T02:57:31Z'  # 12b2
  by: agent  # 12b2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 12b2
  clock: 4  # 12b2
  nonce: 12b2  # 12b2
  message: "SATISFIED by PR #540 (dev bf48544887). Behavioral evidence re-run on the MERGED\ntree, with the item's own filed repro and its control in the same run.\n\n1. The io_mode instance, shipped CLI, control beside it:\n     $ hypergumbo io-boundaries /tmp/iom_c   (read, then truncating write)\n         fs_read  builtins.open\n         fs_write builtins.open          <- was ABSENT before the fix\n     $ hypergumbo io-boundaries /tmp/iom_d   (control: write only)\n         fs_write builtins.open          <- unchanged\n   The truncating write is no longer deleted by a read above it, and the read is\n   not traded away for it -- both crossings are reported, via the plural\n   io_boundaries key INV-zumin already minted.\n\n2. redirect_target, on the filed fixture:\n     before: {'redirect_target': '/dev/null', 'call_lines': [3, 4]}\n     after:  {'redirect_target_values': ['/dev/null', '/etc/cron.d/pwned'],\n              'call_lines': [3, 4]}\n   The singular key is GONE (no consumer can read one site's value as the\n   relationship's) and the cron-dropper is visible.\n\n3. env_var, on the filed fixture:\n     before: {'env_var': 'HOME', 'call_lines': [7, 8]}\n     after:  {'env_var_values': ['API_KEY', 'HOME'], 'call_lines': [7, 8]}\n\nUniform sites are unaffected: redirect_target_resolved stayed singular in (2)\nbecause both sites agreed, which is the contract.\n\nFull affected suite 19869 passed / 0 failed; mypy strict ratchet 669 (+0);\nschema 0.20.3 -> 0.20.4.\n\nCARRIED FORWARD, not closed by this: the item's own \"NOT YET DONE\" note stands\n-- there is no census of which OTHER emitted meta keys are per-call-site. Five\nare declared today (io_mode, call_arg_shape, redirect_target,\nredirect_target_resolved, env_var); those are the ones this investigation\ntouched, not the ones a sweep found. The mechanism now makes declaring a sixth\na one-line change, which is the part that was missing."  # 12b2
